# SRG-APP-000860-WSR-000250  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, allow user
# selection of long passwords and passphrases, including spaces and all
# printable characters.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000860-WSR-000250
group:           V-264351
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004064
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Passwords set through Splunk Web are governed by the same platform
                 settings: the product imposes no maximum length and excludes no printable
                 character, and the configurable share is authentication.conf [splunk_auth]
                 minPasswordLength, which the product STIG sets to 15 or more. The spec's
                 reservation of the semicolon from the special-character rule is the one
                 product limitation on "all printable characters".

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength min 15
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-cloud-platform/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.2.2510/manage-credentials-and-keys/configure-a-splunk-enterprise-password-policy-using-the-authentication.conf-configuration-file
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where authentication is external (LDAP, SAML, ProxySSO) or fronted by an
                 SSO proxy, password length and character set are enforced by that
                 provider.
external:        Browser and workstation handling of spaces and non-ASCII printable
                 characters at the change dialog.
external:        The organization's length policy - organization-defined; the asserted
                 value is the product STIG's.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:441, :477; SPLK-CL-000370 check
                 and fix text
finding:         Passwords set through Splunk Web are not required to be long -
                 authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordLength is missing or 14 or
                 less, leaving the spec default of 8 in force; this determination is from
                 the perspective of the application layer alone, with the semicolon
                 reservation in the special-character rule noted as a product limitation.
